 "best_idea": "Let an NPC take a turn only when it can hear, smell or see the player (or is hurt), and decide fight or flee by comparing level plus HP fraction, so the server spends its per-tick NPC budget only on fights that can happen.",
 "decision": "adapt",
 "decision_why": "Keep the activity gate and the level-plus-HP fight-or-flee test as the brain's cheap first checks (they give a per-tick NPC budget rule and a readable flee rule); drop the stealth-dice wake and the roaming scent trail for a duel, which has one known opponent.",
 "decision_status": "proposed",
 "acceptance": "A server test shows an NPC out of hearing and out of view, at full HP, runs no brain step on that tick; a player entering view makes it act on the same tick; an NPC whose level plus 4 x HP fraction is below the player's moves to flee range once 5 or more units away."
